@startuml folder-tree-structure
title Link — Folder Tree Structure & Share Scope

skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

class "folders (tree)" as tree {
  owner_id : uuid
  parent_id : uuid?
  name : text
}

note as N1
  n-ary tree via self-referencing
  parent_id. Root folders have
  parent_id = NULL.

  Depth limit: 10 levels
  (validated on create/move).
end note
tree .. N1

package "Example ownership tree" {
  folder "Home" as f0
  folder "Work" as f1
  folder "Projects" as f2
  folder "Reading" as f3
  card link1 [GitHub repo]
  card link2 [Design doc]

  f0 --> f1
  f0 --> f3
  f1 --> f2
  f2 --> link1
  f2 --> link2
}

package "Share scope example\n(share on 'Projects')" {
  folder "Projects ✓" as s2 #LightGreen
  card slink1 [GitHub repo] #LightGreen
  card slink2 [Design doc] #LightGreen

  note right of s2
    Visitor sees ONLY this subtree.
    Siblings ("Work", "Reading")
    and their contents are
    invisible — not just locked.
  end note
}

f2 ..> s2 : resolved by\nrecursive CTE

note as N2
  Subtree resolution SQL:

  WITH RECURSIVE subtree AS (
    SELECT id FROM folders WHERE id = $1
    UNION ALL
    SELECT f.id FROM folders f
    JOIN subtree s ON f.parent_id = s.id
  )

  Reused for:
  - share rendering (FR-13)
  - move-cycle prevention (FR-04):
    reject moving X into a
    descendant of X
end note
N2 .. resolve

@enduml
